# Device-specific packages (Google Hayato / MT8192, board google-asurada).
# One package per line; blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.

# firmware
firmware-realtek
firmware-mediatek
firmware-misc-nonfree

# ChromeOS boot chain. These are needed *on the device*, because the card that
# boots from microSD is also the system that installs to and updates the eMMC:
#   cgpt                 writes the ChromeOS GPT (scripts/lib-cgpt.sh)
#   vboot-kernel-utils   provides futility, used to verify the signed kpart
#                        before it is written to the kernel partition
#   depthcharge-tools    provides depthchargectl, which builds the kpart
#                        (scripts/make-kpart.sh) - the same tool boot-deploy
#                        calls on Nura
# Note that cgpt and futility are *separate* Debian packages: vboot-utils only
# ships crossystem and symlinks to futility, so installing it alone leaves both
# cgpt and futility missing.
cgpt
vboot-kernel-utils
depthcharge-tools